                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6b359966-f1cf-3f6c-bb0f-0e984cae22a5",
                        "entry_id": "578e6861-6af5-346b-bf98-16c066229bee",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui révolte ; qui indigne."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "acba7ee7-1514-480b-a4af-3cac5415f783",
                                "sense_id": "6b359966-f1cf-3f6c-bb0f-0e984cae22a5",
                                "text": "Le livre de M. Charles Baudelaire intitulé Les Fleurs du Mal est un défi jeté aux lois qui protègent la religion et la morale. […].A côté de ces pièces et de quelques autres où l’immortalité de l’âme les plus chères croyances du christianisme sont mises à néant, il en est d’autres qui sont l’expression de la lubricité la plus révoltante: […]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f58d51e2-076f-46ce-b2a6-139367645791",
                                "sense_id": "6b359966-f1cf-3f6c-bb0f-0e984cae22a5",
                                "text": "Ces incapables exécuteurs de la loi ne comprennent nullement qu’appliquer la loi sans en comprendre l’esprit, mène tout droit aux désordres. — « La loi le dit, que voulez-vous de plus ? » Ils s’étonnent même sincèrement qu’on exige d’eux, outre l’exécution de la loi, du bon sens et une tête saine. La dernière condition surtout leur parait superflue, elle est pour eux d’un luxe révoltant, cela leur semble une vexation, de l’intolérance."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "243133da-2a96-4614-aa6a-4c54cf4562e4",
                                "sense_id": "6b359966-f1cf-3f6c-bb0f-0e984cae22a5",
                                "text": "Armé d'un chalumeau, le gnome absorbait à même le ruisseau la boisson répandue. C'était grotesque, révoltant."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f8affa7d-3820-46ba-8dfb-23bf0634e70e",
                        "source_entry_id": "578e6861-6af5-346b-bf98-16c066229bee",
                        "source_sense_id": "6b359966-f1cf-3f6c-bb0f-0e984cae22a5",
                        "target_lang_word": "revolting",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "revolting",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4d606769-c2ba-3176-a777-ab9386118d0e",
                                        "entry_id": "3ce07f23-16fb-36dd-8071-91e7b133235f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "present participle and gerund of revolt"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of",
                                            "gerund",
                                            "participle",
                                            "present"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae8b0b80-9a41-41b6-bb86-db09f1719ddb",
                                                "sense_id": "4d606769-c2ba-3176-a777-ab9386118d0e",
                                                "text": "The feudal subjects decided to revolt."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "revolting",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1f3d8178-2653-31c4-8c7d-cc6e207a43ff",
                                        "entry_id": "d9e9b4bd-6f77-3517-9f2c-4f7d6dd3f5e7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "revolution; revolt"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f68ca386-049a-42dc-b64b-a9a2fbc05292",
                                                "sense_id": "1f3d8178-2653-31c4-8c7d-cc6e207a43ff",
                                                "text": "Yet revoltings of the soul would attend this violence to nature, this abuse of physical and intellectual energy, while the beauty of social order would be defaced, and the fountains of earth's felicity broken up."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "revolting",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1401f34c-f9f4-3120-adb3-c281201ee2ca",
                                        "entry_id": "a42afe72-cb1f-3efa-8c8a-7b1063d80157",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "repulsive, disgusting"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c559ec5b-8712-4e09-8a71-14521a6743f0",
                                                "sense_id": "1401f34c-f9f4-3120-adb3-c281201ee2ca",
                                                "text": "The most revolting smell was coming from the drains."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9b2401fb-2215-480b-a69d-65f9547f6f10",
                                                "sense_id": "1401f34c-f9f4-3120-adb3-c281201ee2ca",
                                                "text": "Why anyone should want such a revolting object had always been a mystery to me."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "451456ee-8f93-426e-a440-75853ea50873",
                                                "sense_id": "1401f34c-f9f4-3120-adb3-c281201ee2ca",
                                                "text": "The Leicester Daily Mercury reflected on how these concerns were the result of changing ways of getting around: \"It might sound a bit crazy or just a little revolting that at Christmas works parties, some should drink themselves into a near-insensible state... This was not serious when they used public transport, but today more men and women use their own cars.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
